# Citation metadata for CSANNO software
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'CSANNO: a tiered evidence-mining workflow for molecular activity annotation'
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andre
    name-particle: O
    family-names: Falcao
    email: aofalcao@fc.ul.pt
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3588-8746'
    affiliation: DI/FCUL - Universidade de Lisboa
repository-code: 'https://github.com/aofalcao/mol-activity-annotator'
abstract: >-
  CSANNO is an open-source workflow for retrieving, classifying, aggregating,
  and auditing experimental molecular activity evidence from ChEMBL.
  It reports exact-compound evidence (Tier 0) separately from evidence
  retrieved for structurally similar compounds (Tier 1), and classifies
  retrieved records as active, non-active, or uncertain using configurable
  rules. Gene-centred reports and compound-set summaries preserve evidence
  provenance and support interpretation of target-associated activity.
  CSANNO is an evidence-mining and annotation tool, not a de novo
  target-prediction model.
keywords:
  - Cheminformatics
  - ChEMBL
  - Molecular Activity Annotation
  - Bioactivity Evidence Mining
  - Chemical Similarity
license: MIT
date-released: '2023-06-06'
